<!--
    Stripped Mach-O stubs named from their slot's chained bind
    (`option stubbinds on|off`, default on).

    A `__stubs` entry is named through the LC_DYSYMTAB indirect-symbol table,
    which indexes the undefined nlist of the import it jumps to. A chained-
    fixups link records the import again as the bind on the slot the stub
    loads, so `strip` may drop the nlist and write INDIRECT_SYMBOL_LOCAL | ABS
    over the entry; the SwiftPM frameworks of App Store apps ship that way for
    most of their Swift stdlib and runtime calls. The indirect-symbol walk then
    leaves the stub `sub_<addr>` and every bl to it is an anonymous call.

    Stage / sub-stage: P1 environment-binding. loader/kuna_stubbinds.rs
    decodes each unnamed stub (adrp; ldr; br) to its slot, reads the slot's
    addend-free chained bind and names the stub after the import.

    The XML wrapper only supplies the harness architecture. Both passes clear
    it and load macho_stubs_stripped_arm64 (chkstkdarwin_macho_arm64 with its
    indirect-symbol entries overwritten with LOCAL | ABS; generator
    macho_stubs_stripped_arm64.py) through the object bootstrap. _probe_stub
    calls the __stubs entry at 0x100000520 with bl; the stub loads the __got
    slot at 0x100004000, whose chained bind names ___chkstk_darwin.

    Pass 1 (`option stubbinds off`) reproduces the bug: the call renders
    sub_100000520(...).
    Pass 2 is the shipped default: the stub is __chkstk_darwin, and
    chkstkdarwin (which matches the callee by name) removes the probe call
    from _probe_stub as it does on the unstripped image.

    Assertions span the combined output of both passes.
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x100000" readonly="true">
c0035fd6
</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100000" name="harness_stub"/>
</binaryimage>
<script>
